.TH REGISTRY-CLI 1 "2026-08-25" "registry-cli 1.0.0" "registry-cli manual"
.SH NAME
registry-cli \- manage a static "registrish" Docker/OCI registry
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B registry-cli
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B registry-cli
is a single, fully self-contained (offline-capable) Bash script that manages
a static Docker/OCI registry in the
.B registrish
layout (see
.UR https://github.com/jpetazzo/registrish
.UE ):
a plain
.I v2/<image>/{blobs,manifests}
directory tree that can be served by any static file host \(em Apache2,
NGINX, Netlify, S3, and so on. It never clones a remote repository and does
not depend on any external script: the conversion logic and the Apache
configuration generator are faithful Bash translations of the original
.I dir2reg.sh
and
.I gen-apache2.sh
scripts from the
.I jpetazzo/registrish
repository.
.PP
The tool works with two independent representations of a registry:
.IP \(bu 3
a portable
.B .tar.gz
archive (produced by
.B pull
and consumed by
.BR upload ),
suitable for transferring images to an air-gapped machine;
.IP \(bu 3
a live, on-disk
.B REGISTRY_ROOT
directory (containing
.IR v2/ ,
.I error.json
and
.IR index.html ),
which
.BR upload ", " remove ", " gc ", " sign ", " mirror " and " index
operate on directly, in place.
.SH COMMANDS
.B registry-cli
takes a single subcommand as its first argument, followed by
subcommand-specific options. Every subcommand accepts
.B \-h
or
.B \-\-help
for its full usage text.
.SS "pull \- download an image and produce an archive"
.RS
.B registry-cli pull \-i
.I IMAGE
.B "(\-t"
.I TAG
.B "| \-d"
.IR DIGEST ")"
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B registry-cli pull \-c
.I CONFIG.yaml
.RI [ options ]
.RE
.PP
Downloads one image (single-image mode, using
.BR skopeo )
and packages it as a
.B .tar.gz
archive, or, in multi-image mode
.RB ( \-c / \-\-config ),
synchronizes a whole selection of images/tags described by a
.B skopeo sync
YAML config file (the same format used by
.BR mirror (1))
and bundles all of them into a single archive \(em handy for staging a
transfer to an air-gapped machine, to be
.B upload
ed there afterwards.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-image " " \fIIMAGE\fR
Single-image mode. Image name (e.g.
.IR alpine ,
.IR library/nginx ).
Short names are expanded to their canonical long form by default (e.g.
.I alpine
becomes
.IR docker.io/library/alpine ),
unless
.B \-\-no\-expand
is given.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-tag " " \fITAG\fR
Tag to download. At least one of
.B \-t
/
.B \-d
is required in single-image mode (unless
.BR \-\-from\-dir
is used). Both may be combined: the digest pins the exact content, while
the tag additionally creates a local tag pointer to that same content.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-digest " " \fIDIGEST\fR
Exact digest to download, with or without the
.I sha256:
prefix.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Multi-image mode (mutually exclusive with
.BR \-i / \-t / \-d / \-\-from\-dir ).
.B \-\-arch
/
.B \-\-os
/
.B \-\-source
/
.B \-\-no\-expand
are ignored in this mode (carried by the config file itself instead). If
.B \-o
is omitted, the archive is named
.IR CONFIG\-mirror.tar.gz .
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIARCHIVE\fR
Path of the
.B .tar.gz
archive to produce. If omitted in single-image mode (and without
.BR \-\-to\-dir ),
a name is generated automatically:
.IR IMAGE\-LABEL\-ARCH.tar.gz .
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-to\-dir .
.TP
.BI \-\-to\-dir " DIR"
Instead of an archive, merge the result directly (plain files, additive,
idempotent) into
.IR DIR/v2 .
Meant to be transferred by
.B rsync
with a minimal diff, then ingested with
.BR "upload \-\-from\-dir" .
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-o .
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-gpg\-key " " \fIKEY_ID\fR
Sign each canonical manifest produced with this GPG key, one detached
.I .asc
file per manifest (not a single archive-wide signature; already-signed
manifests are never re-signed; default: unsigned). See the
.B sign
command below.
.TP
.BI \-\-from\-dir " DIR"
Use a directory already produced by
.I "skopeo copy ... dir:DIR"
instead of invoking skopeo \(em enables a fully offline workflow: download
with skopeo on a connected machine, transfer the directory, then package it
here without any network access.
.TP
.BI \-\-source " docker://..."
Skopeo source prefix (default:
.IR docker:// ).
.TP
.BI \-\-arch " ARCH"
Platform architecture to download (default:
.IR amd64 ,
a single platform).
.B \-\-arch all
fetches every platform available in a multi-arch manifest list.
.TP
.BI \-\-os " OS"
Operating system, used together with
.B \-\-arch
(default:
.IR linux ;
ignored with
.IR "\-\-arch all" ).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-expand
Do not expand
.B \-i
/
.B \-\-image
to its canonical long form.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-workdir
Do not delete the temporary working directory (debugging aid).
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-going
Multi-image mode only: passed through to
.IR "skopeo sync \-\-keep\-going" .
.TP
.B \-\-with\-signatures
Look up and bundle, in addition to the image itself (or, in
.B \-c
mode, every synchronized tag, deduplicated by digest), the associated
cosign artifacts: signature
.RI ( sha256\-<digest>.sig ),
attestation
.RI ( .att ,
may embed a CycloneDX SBOM), legacy SBOM
.RI ( .sbom ),
and the static OCI 1.1 "referrers" fallback. Missing artifacts are silently
skipped. Requires
.BR skopeo .
.TP
.BR \-\-sig\-from\-dir " " \fIDIR\fR ", " \-\-att\-from\-dir " " \fIDIR\fR ", " \-\-sbom\-from\-dir " " \fIDIR\fR
Fully offline, per-artifact equivalents (single-image mode only): each
.I DIR
is a
.I "skopeo dir:"
output already produced for the matching companion tag.
.SS "mirror \- synchronize several images/tags into a live registry, in place"
.RS
.B registry-cli mirror \-c
.I CONFIG.yaml
.B \-r
.I REGISTRY_ROOT
.RI [ options ]
.RE
.PP
Unlike
.B pull
(one archive per invocation, uploaded separately),
.B mirror
relies on
.B skopeo sync
to fetch, in one command, a selection of tags spanning several
images/registries, and merges them directly \(em in place, additively,
deduplicated by digest, just like
.BR upload
\(em into a registry that is already being served. Designed to be run
periodically (cron) to keep moving tags such as
.I latest
up to date without re-downloading unchanged content.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Required. YAML file for
.IR "skopeo sync \-\-src yaml" .
Passed through to skopeo verbatim, not interpreted by
.BR registry-cli .
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-registry\-root " " \fIDIR\fR
Required. Registry root to update in place.
.TP
.B \-\-with\-signatures
Also fetch, for every synchronized tag, its associated cosign artifacts
(deduplicated by digest). Disabled by default.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-going
Passed through to
.IR "skopeo sync \-\-keep\-going" .
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Passed through to
.IR "skopeo sync \-\-dry\-run" :
writes nothing to
.IR REGISTRY_ROOT .
.TP
.BR \-\-regen\-config " / " \-\-no\-regen\-config
Regenerate
.I v2/.htaccess
and
.I index.html
after the merge. Enabled by default.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-workdir
Do not delete the temporary working directory.
.PP
Example config file:
.RS
.EX
docker.io:
  images:
    library/alpine:
      \- "3.20"
      \- "latest"
quay.io:
  images:
    coreos/etcd:
      \- latest
.EE
.RE
.SS "upload \- place an archive into a registry"
.RS
.B registry-cli upload \-a
.I ARCHIVE
.B \-r
.I REGISTRY_ROOT
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B "registry-cli upload \-\-from\-dir"
.I DIR
.B \-r
.I REGISTRY_ROOT
.RI [ options ]
.RE
.PP
Verifies the source's checksum (archive mode only), extracts it (archive
mode), or reads it directly with
.B \-\-from\-dir
(read-only), verifies the GPG signature of every signed canonical manifest
it contains (fails and merges nothing if any is invalid), then merges its
files
.RI ( v2/blobs/... ", " v2/manifests/... )
into those already present under
.IR REGISTRY_ROOT/v2 ,
without deleting anything existing.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-archive " " \fIARCHIVE\fR
.B .tar.gz
archive produced by
.BR pull .
Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-from\-dir ;
exactly one of the two is required.
.TP
.BI \-\-from\-dir " DIR"
Directory already produced by
.B "pull \-\-to\-dir"
(or
.BR mirror ),
transferred here as-is (e.g.
.BR rsync ).
Contains
.I v2/...
directly, no archive.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-registry\-root " " \fIDIR\fR
Required. Registry filesystem root.
.TP
.BR \-\-regen\-config " / " \-\-no\-regen\-config
Regenerate
.I v2/.htaccess
after merging. Enabled by default.
.TP
.B \-\-require\-signature
Fail if the archive contains no signed manifest
.RI ( .asc ).
.TP
.B \-\-skip\-checksum
Do not verify the associated
.I .sha256
file.
.TP
.BI \-\-gpg\-keyring " FILE"
Public-key file imported into a temporary keyring for manifest signature
verification.
.SS "list \- inventory of a registry"
.RS
.B registry-cli list \-r
.I REGISTRY_ROOT
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RE
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-registry\-root " " \fIDIR\fR
Required.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit a JSON array instead of a text table.
.SS "remove \- delete a tag, a digest, or a whole image"
.RS
.B registry-cli remove \-r
.I REGISTRY_ROOT
.B \-\-image
.I IMAGE
.RB [ \-\-tag
.I TAG
.B "| \-\-digest"
.IR DIGEST ]
.RI [ options ]
.RE
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-registry\-root " " \fIDIR\fR
Required.
.TP
.BI \-\-image " IMAGE"
Required. Looked up as given first, then, if not found, under its
canonical long name.
.TP
.BI \-\-tag " TAG"
Tag to delete.
.TP
.BI \-\-digest " DIGEST"
Exact digest to delete, targeting
.I manifests/sha256:xxx
directly. Mutually exclusive with
.BR \-\-tag .
If neither
.B \-\-tag
nor
.B \-\-digest
is given, the
.B whole image
is deleted.
.TP
.BR \-\-gc " / " \-\-no\-gc
Clean up this image's manifests/blobs that became orphaned (blobs are
stored per image, so this never affects other images). Enabled by default.
.TP
.BR \-\-purge\-if\-empty " / " \-\-no\-purge\-if\-empty
If no tag remains after deletion, also remove the image directory. Enabled
by default.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Do not prompt for confirmation.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Simulate the operation without deleting anything.
.TP
.BR \-\-regen\-config " / " \-\-no\-regen\-config
Regenerate
.I v2/.htaccess
after deletion. Enabled by default.
.SS "gc \- clean up the whole registry (orphaned manifests/blobs)"
.RS
.B registry-cli gc \-r
.I REGISTRY_ROOT
.RI [ options ]
.RE
.PP
Like
.IR "remove \-\-gc" ,
but across the
.B entire
registry in a single command, without deleting any tag: walks every image
under
.I v2/
and removes manifests/blobs that are no longer reachable from any tag.
Nothing still reachable \(em including cosign companion artifacts
.RI ( .sig / .att / .sbom /
referrers) \(em is ever touched. Meant for routine, periodic (cron) use, or
after several
.IR "remove \-\-no\-gc" .
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-registry\-root " " \fIDIR\fR
Required.
.TP
.BR \-\-purge\-empty\-images " / " \-\-no\-purge\-empty\-images
Also remove the directory of images left with no tag at all (an unusual
situation, usually caused by manual tampering with the registry). Disabled
by default.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Do not prompt for confirmation.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Simulate the cleanup without deleting anything.
.TP
.BR \-\-regen\-config " / " \-\-no\-regen\-config
Regenerate
.I v2/.htaccess
after cleanup. Enabled by default.
.SS "sign \- sign/verify a registry's manifests with GPG"
.RS
.B registry-cli sign \-r
.I REGISTRY_ROOT
.RB ( \-k
.I KEY_ID
.RB "| " \-\-check ")"
.RI [ options ]
.RE
.PP
Signs (or verifies) each
.B canonical
manifest of an already-deployed registry with GPG, one manifest at a time.
Never touches blobs, tag copies, or cosign companion artifacts \(em only
the manifests themselves are signed, which keeps re-signing or later
additions cheap to
.BR rsync .
Useful to sign content added by
.B mirror
(which does not call GPG itself), after a key rotation, or for periodic
integrity checks.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-registry\-root " " \fIDIR\fR
Required.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-gpg\-key " " \fIKEY_ID\fR
Sign every canonical manifest not yet signed with this GPG key.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Sign nothing: verify the
.I .asc
files already present (fail hard if any is invalid). Mutually exclusive
with
.BR \-k .
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-image " " \fIIMAGE\fR
Restrict the operation to this image (path under
.IR v2/ ,
e.g.
.IR library/alpine ).
Repeatable. Default: the whole registry.
.TP
.BI \-\-gpg\-keyring " FILE"
Public-key file imported into a temporary keyring for
.BR \-\-check ,
instead of the user's default GPG keyring.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Re-sign manifests that are already signed (e.g. after a key rotation). No
effect with
.BR \-\-check .
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Show what would be signed/verified without writing anything.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Do not prompt for confirmation.
.TP
.BR \-\-regen\-config " / " \-\-no\-regen\-config
Regenerate
.I v2/.htaccess
after signing. Enabled by default.
.SS "index \- (re)generate the registry's HTML dashboard"
.RS
.B registry-cli index \-r
.I REGISTRY_ROOT
.RE
.PP
Regenerates only the
.I index.html
page at the registry root (a self-contained static dashboard of available
images/tags/architectures), without touching anything else. Useful after a
manual change to the registry, or to generate it for the first time.
Automatically regenerated by
.B upload
and
.B remove
unless
.B \-\-no\-regen\-config
is given.
.SS "verify \- check a cosign signature"
.RS
.B registry-cli verify \-u
.I REGISTRY_URL
.B \-i
.I IMAGE
.B "(\-t"
.I TAG
.B "| \-d"
.IR DIGEST ") \-k"
.I PUBLIC_KEY
.RI [ options ]
.RB [ \-\-
.IR "COSIGN_ARGS..." ]
.RE
.PP
Unlike every other subcommand,
.B verify
never touches a local path: cosign speaks the OCI Distribution HTTP
protocol, so its target must be the URL where
.I v2/
is actually
.B served
(Apache2), not the local filesystem root. Deliberately limited to
public-key verification (no keyless Rekor/Fulcio mode), the only mode
compatible with fully offline use.
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-registry\-url " " \fIHOST[:PORT]\fR
Required. Host of the registry as served over HTTP(S).
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-image " " \fIIMAGE\fR
Required.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-tag " " \fITAG\fR " | " \-d ", " \-\-digest " " \fIDIGEST\fR
Reference to verify (mutually exclusive).
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key " " \fIFILE\fR
Required. Cosign public key
.RI ( cosign.pub ).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-expand
Do not expand
.B \-i
/
.B \-\-image
to its canonical long form.
.TP
.BI \-\- " COSIGN_ARGS..."
Extra cosign arguments passed through verbatim at the end of the command
line.
.SS "sbom \- extract a cosign-attested CycloneDX SBOM"
.RS
.B registry-cli sbom \-u
.I REGISTRY_URL
.B \-i
.I IMAGE
.B "(\-t"
.I TAG
.B "| \-d"
.IR DIGEST ")"
.RI [ options ]
.RB [ \-\-
.IR "COSIGN_ARGS..." ]
.RE
.TP
.BR \-u ", " \-\-registry\-url " " \fIHOST[:PORT]\fR ", " \-i ", " \-\-image " " \fIIMAGE\fR ", " \-t / \-d
Same as
.BR verify .
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key " " \fIFILE\fR
If given, the attestation is
.B verified
.RI ( "cosign verify\-attestation" )
before extraction. Without
.BR \-k ,
the attestation is only
.B downloaded without any verification
.RI ( "cosign download attestation" )
\(em for inspection only, not to be trusted.
.TP
.BI \-\-type " TYPE"
In-toto predicate type to target (default:
.IR cyclonedx ).
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " " \fIFILE\fR
Output file (default: stdout).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-expand
Do not expand
.B \-i
/
.B \-\-image
to its canonical long form.
.TP
.BI \-\- " COSIGN_ARGS..."
Extra cosign arguments passed through verbatim.
.PP
Requires
.B jq
(mandatory, no grep/sed fallback: correctly decoding a nested base64 DSSE
envelope without risking corrupting the SBOM needs a real JSON parser). If
several attestations of the same type exist for the image, only the first
one is extracted.
.SS "completion \- print the bash completion script"
.RS
.B registry-cli completion
.RE
.PP
Prints a bash completion script to stdout. Temporary use:
.IR "source <(registry-cli completion)" .
Permanent install:
.IR "registry-cli completion > /etc/bash_completion.d/registry-cli" .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I REGISTRY_ROOT/v2/<image>/manifests/
Tag files (plain copies of the manifest JSON) and content-addressed
.I sha256:<digest>
canonical manifests.
.TP
.I REGISTRY_ROOT/v2/<image>/blobs/
Content-addressed
.I sha256:<digest>
layer/config blobs.
.TP
.IR REGISTRY_ROOT/v2/.htaccess " , " REGISTRY_ROOT/v2/error.json
Apache2 configuration generated by
.BR upload / remove / gc / mirror / index
(see the "Serving the registry with Apache2" section of the project
README).
.TP
.I REGISTRY_ROOT/index.html
Self-contained static HTML dashboard, regenerated by the same commands.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B 0
on success,
.B 1
on any error (invalid arguments, missing dependency, network/skopeo
failure, checksum/signature mismatch, and so on).
.SH DEPENDENCIES
Hard requirements: a POSIX shell toolchain
.RI ( bash ", " tar ", " sha256sum ", " find ", " grep ", " sed ),
.B rsync
(used by
.BR upload " to merge archives), and " jq
(used throughout for JSON parsing; a grep/sed fallback exists for most
operations but is not used by
.BR sbom ,
which requires
.BR jq ).
Optional, feature-gated dependencies:
.B skopeo
(required by
.BR pull / mirror
whenever network access is used, i.e. without
.BR \-\-from\-dir ),
.B gpg
(archive signing/verification), and
.B cosign
(required by
.BR verify " and " sbom ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR skopeo (1),
.BR skopeo\-sync (1),
.BR skopeo\-copy (1),
.BR cosign (1),
.BR gpg (1),
.BR rsync (1),
.BR jq (1)
.PP
